.TH QLEVER\-UI 8 "2026-03-12" "qlever-ui" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
qlever\-ui \- QLever UI web application administration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qlever\-ui
is a Django/gunicorn web application managed by systemd.
This manual describes how to expose it via a reverse proxy or directly on a TCP port.
.SH DESCRIPTION
By default,
.B qlever\-ui
binds to a Unix domain socket at
.IR /run/qlever\-ui/qlever\-ui.sock .
It is not directly reachable from the network.
A reverse proxy such as nginx or Apache is the recommended way to expose it.
.PP
Example configurations for both are installed in
.IR /usr/share/qlever\-ui/ .
.SH ACTIVATION WITH NGINX
.SS Required modules
nginx must have
.B proxy
and
.B proxy_http
support compiled in (the default in Debian packages).
.SS Steps
.TP
1.
Enable the example configuration:
.PP
.RS
.EX
cp /usr/share/qlever\-ui/qlever\-ui\-nginx.conf \\
   /etc/nginx/sites\-available/qlever\-ui.conf
ln \-s /etc/nginx/sites\-available/qlever\-ui.conf \\
   /etc/nginx/sites\-enabled/
.EE
.RE
.TP
2.
Set
.B server_name
to your hostname by editing
.IR /etc/nginx/sites\-available/qlever\-ui.conf .
.TP
3.
Test and reload nginx:
.PP
.RS
.EX
nginx \-t
systemctl reload nginx
.EE
.RE
.SH ACTIVATION WITH APACHE
.SS Required modules
.EX
a2enmod proxy proxy_http headers
.EE
.SS Steps
.TP
1.
Enable the example configuration:
.PP
.RS
.EX
cp /usr/share/qlever\-ui/qlever\-ui\-apache.conf \\
   /etc/apache2/sites\-available/qlever\-ui.conf
a2ensite qlever\-ui
.EE
.RE
.TP
2.
Set
.B ServerName
to your hostname by editing
.IR /etc/apache2/sites\-available/qlever\-ui.conf .
.TP
3.
Reload Apache:
.PP
.RS
.EX
systemctl reload apache2
.EE
.RE
.SH RUNNING DIRECTLY ON A TCP PORT
If you prefer to expose
.B qlever\-ui
directly on a TCP port without a reverse proxy, you must override the
service configuration.
.TP
1.
Create a systemd drop\-in:
.PP
.RS
.EX
systemctl edit qlever\-ui.service
.EE
.RE
.TP
2.
Add the following (replacing
.I 8176
with your desired port):
.PP
.RS
.EX
[Service]
ExecStart=
ExecStart=/opt/venvs/qlever\-ui/bin/gunicorn qlever.wsgi:application \\
    \-\-bind 0.0.0.0:8176 \\
    \-\-workers 4 \-\-timeout 120 \\
    \-\-access\-logfile /var/log/qlever\-ui/access.log \\
    \-\-error\-logfile /var/log/qlever\-ui/error.log \\
    \-\-limit\-request\-line 10000
.EE
.RE
.PP
The empty
.B ExecStart=
line clears the default value before setting the new one.
.TP
3.
Disable the socket unit (no longer needed) and restart the service:
.PP
.RS
.EX
systemctl disable \-\-now qlever\-ui.socket
systemctl restart qlever\-ui.service
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/qlever\-ui/qlever\-ui.env
Runtime environment variables (Django settings, allowed hosts, etc.).
.TP
.I /var/lib/qlever\-ui/qleverui.sqlite3
Application database.
.TP
.I /var/log/qlever\-ui/
Access and error logs.
.TP
.I /run/qlever\-ui/qlever\-ui.sock
Unix domain socket (created at service start).
.TP
.I /usr/share/qlever\-ui/qlever\-ui\-nginx.conf
Example nginx reverse\-proxy configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/share/qlever\-ui/qlever\-ui\-apache.conf
Example Apache reverse\-proxy configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nginx (8),
.BR apache2 (8),
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR systemd.socket (5)
